00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.630 align:start position:0%
at the agriculture and Fisheries Council  on the 14th of July the Italian  presidency will set out its work program  priorities for the next six months there  will be a debate on organic farming  following the presentation of a proposal  in March for a review of the legislation  concerning organic production and  farming in Europe the debate will focus  on which elements of flexibility should  be introduced how more effective and  targeted controls should be put in place  and the type of delegated act to  consider at this council that could be  agreement on the way forwards for the  dairy sector if diverging positions  amongst member states are resolved some  Member States urge for additional  measures before the end of the quota  system next year in order to ensure a  proper soft landing or a more  economically gentle transition whilst  other member states are asking for  measures for the future of the sector to  avoid a crisis after the end of the  quota system regarding fisheries there  will be an exchange of views between  ministers based on the Commission's  proposals concerning total allowable  catches for 2015 this includes the state  of the stocks and a limited overview of  the economic performance of the EU fleet  it also takes into account as agreed in  the reformed Common Fisheries Policy the  upcoming landing obligation where  oarfish court must be brought ashore and  counted as part of the total catch this  will pave the way for decisions to be  made on specific fish stocks later in  the year  I
 

